WEBVTT

00:00:00.642 --> 00:00:01.550
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.779 --> 00:00:04.109
Today I hope you will listen to the very end,

00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:07.150
even those of you who have been in the trade for many years.

00:00:07.536 --> 00:00:10.590
Because this lesson is not about making clients beautiful.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.030
It is about this:

00:00:12.523 --> 00:00:15.870
ten years from now, will you still be able to do this work?

00:00:16.484 --> 00:00:19.310
We are talking about allergies, and about chemicals.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.593
There is a story we hear very often in this trade.

00:00:22.854 --> 00:00:25.553
A skilled nail technician, with lots of clients.

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:30.273
At first, it is just itching on the fingertips, and a few small blisters.

00:00:30.598 --> 00:00:33.073
She thinks it comes from washing her hands so much.

00:00:33.494 --> 00:00:36.779
A few months later, her eyelids become red and swollen,

00:00:36.729 --> 00:00:39.073
even though gel never touched her eyes.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.393
At the doctor, she finds out:

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.473
she has become allergic to gel.

00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:47.393
From then on, the slightest touch of uncured gel brings it back.

00:00:47.712 --> 00:00:50.033
Some people have had to leave the trade because of this.

00:00:50.629 --> 00:00:52.838
First, we need to tell two things apart.

00:00:53.451 --> 00:00:55.878
Irritation is direct damage to the skin:

00:00:56.144 --> 00:00:58.438
from water, soap, acetone.

00:00:58.864 --> 00:01:02.118
Stop the contact, care for the skin, and it heals.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.638
Allergy is different.

00:01:04.073 --> 00:01:08.038
The immune system has memorized a substance, and treats it as an enemy.

00:01:08.308 --> 00:01:14.358
From then on, even a tiny amount causes itching, redness, blisters, swelling.

00:01:14.536 --> 00:01:17.723
The reaction often comes late, one to three days later,

00:01:17.673 --> 00:01:20.118
so many people do not know what caused it.

00:01:20.362 --> 00:01:21.959
It can also show up somewhere else:

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:26.310
the eyelids, the face, the neck, because your hands touch them,

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.838
or because dust and vapor drift there.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:32.676
The scariest thing is that an allergy gives no warning.

00:01:33.084 --> 00:01:36.436
You can work with gel for five years with no problem at all.

00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:41.396
But every time uncured product touches the skin, the body records a little more.

00:01:41.739 --> 00:01:44.276
Then one day, it crosses the threshold.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:47.236
And once you are allergic, it is usually for life.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:48.996
There is only one way left:

00:01:49.182 --> 00:01:51.156
avoid that substance completely.

00:01:51.792 --> 00:01:54.697
So which substances cause allergies most often?

00:01:55.158 --> 00:01:57.577
In nails, it is the acrylate family.

00:01:58.006 --> 00:02:02.617
They are in gel polish, builder gel, acrylic liquid, and nail glue.

00:02:03.046 --> 00:02:06.457
While they are liquid and uncured, they are strong allergens.

00:02:06.783 --> 00:02:09.257
Once fully cured, they are almost harmless.

00:02:09.558 --> 00:02:11.671
So the risk lies in uncured product,

00:02:11.621 --> 00:02:14.937
and in the filing dust from gel that was not fully cured.

00:02:15.495 --> 00:02:16.396
In lashes:

00:02:16.505 --> 00:02:20.236
lash glue is cyanoacrylate, the same family as super glue.

00:02:20.746 --> 00:02:24.594
The glue gives off fumes that sting the eyes, cause a runny nose,

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:25.996
and can cause allergies.

00:02:26.308 --> 00:02:28.755
For the client, and also for the technician,

00:02:28.705 --> 00:02:31.916
who leans in close over the glue drop for hours every day.

00:02:32.425 --> 00:02:35.516
A glue labeled as sensitive is still the same substance.

00:02:36.046 --> 00:02:38.761
With hair dye, lash tint and brow tint,

00:02:38.711 --> 00:02:43.680
the main culprit is a coloring agent called PPD, and related substances.

00:02:44.194 --> 00:02:47.920
This kind of allergy can be very severe, with the whole face swelling.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.560
There is one question worth asking the client:

00:02:51.063 --> 00:02:53.280
have you ever had a black henna tattoo on holiday?

00:02:53.549 --> 00:02:56.720
Because black henna is often mixed with this very substance.

00:02:57.021 --> 00:03:00.560
Hair bleach powder rises into the air, as a fine dust.

00:03:00.815 --> 00:03:05.496
Breathed in over a long time, it can make the technician sneeze, wheeze,

00:03:05.446 --> 00:03:07.040
and even develop asthma.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:10.160
There are also fragrances, and latex gloves.

00:03:10.721 --> 00:03:11.684
How do we prevent it?

00:03:12.003 --> 00:03:12.964
Rule number one:

00:03:13.197 --> 00:03:15.524
uncured product never touches the skin.

00:03:15.951 --> 00:03:18.244
Leave a small gap from the skin when you paint.

00:03:18.513 --> 00:03:22.164
If some gets on the skin, wipe it off before the hand goes into the lamp.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.499
Wipe the bottle neck, the brush handle and the table clean,

00:03:25.449 --> 00:03:28.244
because those are the places your hands touch all day.

00:03:28.672 --> 00:03:30.244
Next, rule number two:

00:03:30.512 --> 00:03:31.364
cure fully.

00:03:31.521 --> 00:03:35.124
The right lamp for the brand, the full time, and thin coats.

00:03:35.702 --> 00:03:36.663
Rule number three:

00:03:37.002 --> 00:03:39.383
wear nitrile gloves, and change them often.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.143
Then rule number four:

00:03:41.332 --> 00:03:42.423
keep the air clean.

00:03:42.684 --> 00:03:45.463
Switch on the table extraction when you file or drill.

00:03:45.732 --> 00:03:46.903
Open the ventilation.

00:03:47.172 --> 00:03:49.383
Close the bottle right after taking product.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:50.983
Use a bin with a lid.

00:03:51.491 --> 00:03:57.383
The City of Helsinki guidance requires that an acrylic nail station has local exhaust ventilation that is strong enough.

00:03:58.084 --> 00:04:00.044
Finally, rule number five:

00:04:00.313 --> 00:04:01.644
know what you are using.

00:04:02.238 --> 00:04:05.964
Buy from suppliers within Europe, with a label and an ingredient list.

00:04:06.352 --> 00:04:10.764
In the European Union, nail products containing HEMA must state on the label:

00:04:10.872 --> 00:04:14.284
for professional use only, and can cause an allergic reaction.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:20.124
And TPO has been banned completely in nail products since 1 September 2025.

00:04:20.352 --> 00:04:23.724
Salons may not keep using it, not even stock bought before.

00:04:23.985 --> 00:04:27.484
You should also ask your supplier for the safety data sheet of each product.

00:04:27.817 --> 00:04:30.844
It states which gloves you need, and what first aid to give.

00:04:31.436 --> 00:04:33.966
About testing for a reaction before the service.

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:39.814
For hair dye, lash tint and brow tint, many brands require a skin test beforehand,

00:04:39.764 --> 00:04:42.286
usually 48 hours before the service.

00:04:42.551 --> 00:04:46.446
Follow the instructions of the brand exactly, and write down the test date.

00:04:46.843 --> 00:04:51.486
In Europe, the labels of many hair dyes and lash tints must also carry a warning:

00:04:51.677 --> 00:04:53.937
can cause severe allergic reactions,

00:04:53.887 --> 00:04:57.006
and not intended for use on persons under sixteen.

00:04:57.317 --> 00:04:58.366
But please remember:

00:04:58.715 --> 00:05:01.966
a test with no reaction does not mean it is safe forever.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:07.006
And a client who has ever reacted to a dye, or to black henna, is not treated.

00:05:07.627 --> 00:05:09.806
If a client reacts during the service:

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:13.406
itching, burning, redness, swelling.

00:05:13.832 --> 00:05:14.926
Stop immediately.

00:05:15.342 --> 00:05:19.886
Remove the product from the skin very gently, then rinse with plenty of water.

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:24.446
If it gets in the eye, rinse the eye with clean water for several minutes.

00:05:24.873 --> 00:05:26.696
Advise the client to see a doctor,

00:05:26.646 --> 00:05:29.566
and give them the product name and its ingredient list,

00:05:29.597 --> 00:05:30.686
so the doctor knows.

00:05:31.028 --> 00:05:35.966
And if the client has trouble breathing, swollen lips or face, or feels faint:

00:05:36.223 --> 00:05:38.286
call emergency services right away.

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:43.246
In the European Union, the common emergency number is 112.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.724
And if it is you who is affected:

00:05:45.947 --> 00:05:49.484
do not hide it, and do not treat yourself and carry on working.

00:05:49.959 --> 00:05:51.564
See a dermatologist early.

00:05:51.993 --> 00:05:56.204
The doctor can do a patch test, to find the exact substance you are allergic to.

00:05:56.557 --> 00:05:59.140
Find out early, change the way you work early,

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.564
and many people manage to stay in the trade.

00:06:01.911 --> 00:06:03.004
And keep records.

00:06:03.101 --> 00:06:04.444
In the file of each client:

00:06:04.684 --> 00:06:08.604
what the client is allergic to, the test date, the products used.

00:06:09.108 --> 00:06:10.124
If there is an incident:

00:06:10.289 --> 00:06:14.684
write down the date, the product name, the batch number, and how you handled it.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:18.701
You know, an occupational allergy is not bad luck.

00:06:18.955 --> 00:06:22.621
Most of it can be prevented, with small habits repeated every day.

00:06:23.099 --> 00:06:27.261
Rules on chemicals differ from country to country, so check again where you work.

00:06:27.672 --> 00:06:31.821
Protecting your hands, and protecting your breathing, is protecting your career.

00:06:32.157 --> 00:06:34.861
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
